# The glossary: what the words the manual uses mean. Link to a term from any text with
# [[its name]].

Term: ACRO
  The rate mode of the sim. The sticks set the rate of roll and pitch. When you centre the
  sticks, the plane holds its attitude. Use it for aerobatics.

Term: ANGLE
  The self-levelling mode of the sim. The sticks set the angle of bank and pitch. When you
  release the sticks, the plane becomes level. Use it when you learn to fly.

Term: ArduPilot
  The open-source autopilot. ArduPlane is its version for planes. Here, it runs as
  [[SITL]] and flies the plane of the sim. The [[Ground control station]] talks to it.

Term: Annunciator
  A lamp on the CAUTION / WARNING screen of the ground station. ARMED lights when the plane
  is armed. Other lamps show the link, GPS, the battery, a stall and the fence.

Term: AUTO
  The mode of ArduPilot that flies the [[mission]] on the vehicle, one item after the other.

Term: Chase
  The view from just behind the plane, following it.

Term: Current item
  The [[mission]] item that the plane flies to in AUTO. The map shows it in magenta. WP1
  sends the plane back to the first item.

Term: Differential thrust
  When you use the rudder, one motor turns faster and the other turns more slowly. Thus the
  plane turns more quickly in yaw than with the rudder only. X turns it on and off.

Term: FBWA
  Fly By Wire A, a mode of ArduPilot. The sticks set the angle of bank and pitch, and the
  autopilot holds them. It is like ANGLE in the sim.

Term: FPV
  First-person view: the picture from a camera in the nose of the plane. The camera points
  20° up.

Term: GUIDED
  The mode of ArduPilot that flies the plane to one point. GOTO on the map puts the plane in
  GUIDED.

Term: Hand launch
  A launch where you throw the plane into the air. The plane does not use a runway. You
  launch the T1-S in this way, and also the plane in the sim.

Term: HUD
  The text on the view of the sim. The top line shows the flight mode, the rates and
  differential thrust. The
  lines below it show the controller, the view, the throttle, the speeds, the height, the
  attitude, the battery and the wind. Messages such as CRASHED and PAUSED (P) appear in the
  middle.

Term: Home
  The point where you armed the plane. RTL brings the plane back to it. The map shows it.

Term: Line of sight
  The view from the [[pilot box]]. You look at the plane as you do at the field. The HUD
  calls it LINE OF SIGHT, and the help screen calls it LOS.

Term: LOITER
  A mode of ArduPilot, and a mission item, that circles a point.

Term: MANUAL
  In the sim, the mode where the sticks move the control surfaces directly. Nothing helps
  you. In ArduPilot, the mode where the autopilot sends the sticks directly to the plane.

Term: MAVLink
  The protocol that ArduPilot and ground stations use to talk to each other.

Term: Remote ID
  A broadcast that an unmanned aircraft sends on Bluetooth or Wi-Fi. It says who the aircraft
  is and where it is, about once a second. Any receiver near the aircraft can read it. The
  standard is ASTM F3411. Many countries ask for it.

Term: Telemetry link
  The radio link that brings the data of the plane to the station. The station gets it from
  the TX15. The link is narrow, so the plane sends its own data first.

Term: Marker
  The symbol of another plane on the [[tactical map]]. A live marker is bright. A stale marker
  is dim and stays where the plane was last heard.

Term: Mission
  The list of items that the autopilot flies in AUTO: waypoints, loiters, a takeoff, a
  landing or a return home. The map shows the mission on the vehicle as a solid line.

Term: Pilot box
  The place where you stand at the field to fly. The sim starts there, with the plane in
  your hand.

Term: Pitch stick
  The stick that moves the nose up and down. On the keyboard, W pushes it forward (nose down)
  and S pulls it back (nose up).

Term: Plan
  The mission that you edit in the ground station. The map shows it as a dashed line. When
  you upload it, it becomes the mission on the vehicle.

Term: Plan altitude
  The height above home for new waypoints. It shows between ALT- and ALT+.

Term: Roll stick
  The stick that banks the plane. On the keyboard, A rolls the plane to the left and D rolls
  it to the right.

Term: Rates
  How far the control surfaces move for a movement of the stick. High rates give tight
  turns. Low rates give gentle turns. L changes between them.

Term: RTL
  Return to launch: ArduPilot flies the plane back to [[home]]. RTL is also a mission item
  that does the same.

Term: Sensor feed
  The window that shows the picture from the camera below the nose of the plane, with the
  sensor symbols on it. The ground station can point the camera.

Term: SITL
  Software in the loop. ArduPilot runs on your computer, not on a flight controller. The sim
  gives it the physics and the sensors of the plane.

Term: Tactical map
  The map of the valley in the ground station, on the screen with the title TACTICAL
  SITUATION. It shows the plane, home, the plan and the mission on the vehicle.

Term: Waypoint
  A point that the plane flies to, at a set height. Most items in a mission are waypoints.

Term: VTOL
  An aircraft that takes off and lands vertically (Vertical Take-Off and Landing), like a
  copter, and flies forward on its wing, like a plane. The T1-S VTOL is one.

Term: tilt-rotor
  A motor that can turn between pointing up and pointing forward. In a hover it lifts the
  plane like a copter rotor. In forward flight it pushes the plane like the motor of a plane.

Term: transition
  The change between a hover and forward flight. The plane does it while it flies: the wing
  motors tilt, and the wing takes the weight from the rotors, or gives it back.

Term: Computer pilot
  An opponent in the games that the sim flies. Each computer pilot flies a T1-S on the same
  physics as your plane, and has its own skill. Kestrel is an ace, Merlin flies at a club
  level and Swift is a rookie.

Term: Pylon race
  A race round a triangle of three [[pylons]], as in the pylon racing leagues. G starts one.
  Five laps make a race. The first pilot across the start line after the last lap wins.

Term: Pylon
  A tall marker on the field. In a [[pylon race]], the three pylons mark the turns of the
  course. Fly round the outside of each one.

Term: Cut
  A turn inside a pylon in a [[pylon race]]. One cut adds 10 % to your time. Two cuts
  disqualify you.

Term: Tag
  A game where one plane is [[it]] and chases the others. When it touches another plane, that
  plane is it. T starts one.

Term: It
  The plane that chases the others in a game of [[tag]]. The pilot who is it for the least
  time wins.

Term: Arena
  The part of the sky for a game of [[tag]]: a circle of 90 m round the centre of the field,
  below 60 m. Small cones mark its edge. If you fly out of it, you are [[it]].

Term: Flight computer
  The device between the TX15 and the autopilot. The TX15 sends it the stick and switch channels on a serial line. It passes them on to [[ArduPilot]] as the radio channels, and it sends the plane's state back to the TX15. In the sim, a simulated flight computer does this.

Term: CRSF
  The serial protocol of ExpressLRS radio links. The TX15 and the [[flight computer]] use it on their serial line: channels one way, telemetry and MAVLink the other.
